And now we go fifty years in the future and we use what we know about what the population, the makeup of the United States population is gonna look like in fifty years.

67
00:07:41,200 --> 00:07:41,520
Yes.

68
00:07:41,520 --> 00:07:59,600
And we can volve those data sets and what they found was that if the makeup of these um degree granting programs doesn't change, that we're actually gonna be graduating t uh nine percent less people in science and engineering in the year twenty fifty than we are now.

